 "readme": {
  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "SIC existence in Lean",
  "excerpt": "A [symmetric informationally complete measurement (SIC)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SIC-POVM) is a highly symmetric quantum measurement built from $d^2$ states in dimension $d$, with every distinct pair having the same overlap. This is equivalent to $d^2$ equiangular lines in $\\mathbb C^d$. Zauner's conjecture asks whether SICs exist in every finite dimension."
 },
